<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  "Which signing route?" — Gateway_SigningRoute in qa-report-signing.bpmn.

  From the owner, 2026-09-20 on #363:

    | in this case an API wouldnt wokr and a human actor is needed. so
    | process for signing needs two parallel routes/processes, air gapped
    | vs not, the first needed a human actor

  Two facts, and they answer different questions:

    reach                  effectiveReach(deployment, actor) from
                           `schemas/actor-reach.ts` — CAN this participant
                           call out at all. One of internet,
                           egress-restricted, air-gapped, unknown.
    signingApiConfigured   the `signing-api` capability probe — IS there an
                           endpoint to call. A boolean, from configuration,
                           not from a live request.

  Neither substitutes for the other, which is why both columns exist. A
  configured endpoint on an air-gapped host is still uncallable; a connected
  host with nothing configured has nothing to call.

  ## `unknown` routes to the human, and that is the load-bearing row

  A gateway that read "could not determine" as "use the API" would fail
  CLOSED ON THE WIRE AND OPEN IN THE RECORD: the call fails, and what
  survives is a QA report that nobody signed and nothing says is unsigned.
  Routing it to a person costs a signature request and cannot produce that
  outcome. Same rule as `ci-health` — could-not-check is never green.

  ## `egress-restricted` is not decided by reach alone

  It means SOME egress is blocked, not which. So it is admitted only in the
  row that also has an endpoint configured, and the operator's allowlist is
  what makes that true. If the call then fails, the process re-enters here
  with the actor's reach corrected — a declaration fix, not a retry.

  ## What is deliberately NOT a column

  Whether the report is worth signing. That is the QA verdict, already
  computed upstream by `draft-qa-gate.dmn`, and a table that re-decided it
  would be a second answer free to disagree with the first.
-->
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/"
             id="Definitions_SigningRoute"
             name="Signing route"
             namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/decisions">
  <decision id="Decision_SigningRoute" name="Which signing route?">
    <decisionTable id="Table_SigningRoute" hitPolicy="FIRST">
      <input id="In_Reach" label="performing actor's effective reach">
        <inputExpression id="Expr_Reach" typeRef="string">
          <text>reach</text>
        </inputExpression>
      </input>
      <input id="In_ApiConfigured" label="signing endpoint configured">
        <inputExpression id="Expr_ApiConfigured" typeRef="boolean">
          <text>signingApiConfigured</text>
        </inputExpression>
      </input>
      <output id="Out_Route" name="outcome" typeRef="string" />

      <rule id="Rule_AirGapped">
        <description>An air-gapped actor cannot call any endpoint, however well configured.</description>
        <inputEntry id="IE_Air_1"><text>"air-gapped"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="IE_Air_2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="OE_Air"><text>"human"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="Rule_Unknown">
        <description>Reach undeclared. Could-not-determine takes the route that needs no network.</description>
        <inputEntry id="IE_Unk_1"><text>"unknown"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="IE_Unk_2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="OE_Unk"><text>"human"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="Rule_NoEndpoint">
        <description>Reachable, but nothing is configured to call.</description>
        <inputEntry id="IE_NoEp_1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="IE_NoEp_2"><text>false</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="OE_NoEp"><text>"human"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="Rule_Api">
        <description>Can call out, and has an endpoint. The only row that reaches the API.</description>
        <inputEntry id="IE_Api_1"><text>"internet", "egress-restricted"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="IE_Api_2"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="OE_Api"><text>"api"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="Rule_Default">
        <description>Anything the rows above do not name — including a reach value added to the vocabulary and not yet given a row. It routes to a person rather than to the wire, so an unhandled value degrades into a slower signature and never into an unsigned report.</description>
        <inputEntry id="IE_Def_1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="IE_Def_2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="OE_Def"><text>"human"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
    </decisionTable>
  </decision>
</definitions>
